# PHASE 2 — AUTONOMOUS TOPIC SELECTION & DUPLICATE PREVENTION

## A. Topics AI khud select kare

Har din topics manually provide karne ki zaroorat na ho. System automatically eligible topics select kare aur daily schedule ke mutabiq publishing workflow chalaye.

AI ko sirf random titles generate nahin karne. Topic selection mein yeh factors hon:

- Existing app ke actual functions aur feature catalog.
- Services, courses, tools, learning resources aur tutorials.
- Public ke practical problems aur useful solutions.
- Kids learning, Urdu/English, stories, activities aur relevant educational subjects.
- Topic ki historical promotion frequency.
- Topic recently publish hua hai ya nahin.
- Primary vs Secondary ka purpose.
- Selected YouTube Short ka actual subject, jahan applicable ho.

Primary Marketing direct app/service value explain karega; Secondary Marketing pehle reader ko independent value dega aur phir relevant CTA naturally include karega.

## B. Topic history permanent rakhein

Persistent topic history/ledger zaroori hai, taake restart, manual run, failed run ya trigger recreation se rotation reset na ho.

Har content record mein kam az kam yeh save ho:

- Unique content/topic ID.
- Normalized topic identity aur category.
- Slot aur destination blog.
- Resource type: `POST` ya `PAGE`.
- Related app feature, agar applicable ho.
- Selected YouTube Video ID, agar applicable ho.
- Content identity/hash.
- Existing/published Blogger object ID aur URL.
- Scheduled, started, published timestamps.
- Status, error aur retry history.
- Last-used topic date aur cooldown/rotation eligibility.

Same day ke 6 outputs mein meaningfully duplicate topics allowed nahin hain. Topic sirf title badal kar repeat na ho. Previous days ki history se bhi recently used topics avoid hon.

Cooldown/rotation policy configurable ho. Naya ya pehle kabhi promote na hua relevant topic preference le. Kids content ki priority maintain ho, magar har article ko Kids topic mein force na kiya jaye.

Agar unique, useful content ke liye valid topic ya source available na ho to duplicate/thin content publish karne ke bajaye retry aur explicit failure report karein.

## C. Double posting ko fail-safe tareeqe se rokna

Blogger Posts aur Pages alag resource types hain; har relevant destination ko separately check karna hoga.

Publish karne se pehle:

1. Correct blog identity verify karein.
2. Existing Blogger Posts/Pages aur persistent ledger se canonical content identity check karein.
3. YouTube-based content ke liye actual Video ID/URL match karein.
4. Topic ID/hash aur normalized title/content ko secondary checks ke taur par use karein.
5. Check karein ke same automation item pehle se published, in-progress ya queued to nahin.
6. Concurrent manual/automatic execution ko locking/idempotency se prevent karein.

**Agar duplicate pre-check fail ho, blog/API request 403/404 de, wrong identity mile, backend HTML return kare, ya result uncertain ho, to publishing rok dein.**

Error ko ignore karke new content publish karna prohibited hai.

Agar Blogger publication succeed ho jaye magar ledger save fail ho, to recovery logic pehle Blogger par existing published item locate kare aur uska returned ID/URL ledger mein recover kare. Dobara publish na kare.

User ne blogs manually clear kiye hain. Iska matlab yeh nahin ke deduplication ki zaroorat khatam ho gayi. Ab permanent cross-run duplicate protection aur sahi topic rotation implement karna hai.

